---
# ansible-lint configuration.
#
# The CI workflow runs `ansible-lint --profile production`; the profile is
# passed explicitly there and is not set here.
#
# The list below is deliberately empty. It held three entries -- for
# verify-recipe-custom.yml, verify-recipe-fuzz.yml and verify-recipe-edges.yml
# -- because those ladders called `catalog` and `api_key` before either module
# was in the collection. #32 and #30 landed them and all three came off. Every
# file in the repository is linted.
#
# Before adding one back: `syntax-check` cannot be waived inline, because it
# comes from ansible-playbook's own parser rather than from lint, so
# `# noqa: syntax-check[unknown-module]` has no effect. That is the pressure
# that produced the three entries above. If you need one again, pair it with a
# self-expiring entry in tests/unit/test_module_references.py, so the waiver
# cannot outlive its reason -- that is how these three expired on schedule
# rather than becoming permanent.
exclude_paths: []
